      "section_title": "What is metoprolol?",
      "line_start": 6,
      "line_end": 6,
      "evidence_char_start": 322,
      "evidence_char_end": 754,
      "evidence_text": "Metoprolol works by blocking the effect of adrenaline and noradrenaline on beta-1 receptors in your heart. This slows your heart rate, reduces how hard your heart squeezes, and lowers your blood pressure. Because the heart is doing less work, it needs less oxygen, which is why metoprolol also helps with angina. Exactly how metoprolol works for high blood pressure, heart failure, and after a heart attack is not fully understood.\n",
      "additional_context": [],
